{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Opened the recovery and resynchronization mechanism, which the audit had not yet covered: whether a snapshot restore can leave raft membership stale relative to the restored log. Recorded a refuted result. restore rejects out-of-date snapshots, refuses role downgrades, and sets the log's committed and processed positions; restoreRemotes rebuilds all three role maps from the snapshot membership rather than merging, so an absent node cannot be counted in a later quorum and a removed leader steps down. The running follower reaches that replacement through the state machine's Recover task, and the interim window is closed for elections by the committed-versus-applied gate. Added six source ranges, one behavior entry, the question and its interpretation, with the non-atomic ordering and supervisor dependence kept as counterevidence and limits. Validation reports valid, no_change false, no execution requested.\"}"}}
